<p><strong>Asteroid Search Campaigns help scientists</strong> <strong>to discover new asteroids </strong> <strong>and track them and possibly to prevent unwanted impacts with the Earth</strong> <strong>but also study their composition and the origins of our Solar System.</strong></p>
<p>International Asteroid Day, on June 30, is to commemorate the Tunguska impact,  also known as the Tunguska event which occured in 1908. </p>
<p>On that day a large explosion occurred in the sky over the Podkamennaya Tunguska River in Siberia, Russia.</p>
<p>It destroyed about 2,000 square kilometers of the forest in the area, flattening about 80 million trees.</p>
<p>It is thought that an asteroid or a comet was responsible for the blast. </p>
<p>The Tunguska event is considered to be the largest asteroid impact on Earth in recorded history.</p>
